---
source: crates/jailint/tests/rules.rs
---
error[min_max]: this is always `0`: the bounds are swapped
  --> tests/lint/min_max/bad.jai:5:10
   |
 5 |     a := min(0, max(100, x));
   |          ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
help: to keep a value between 0 and 100, write `clamp(value, 0, 100)`
   |
 4       x := 50;
 5 ~     a := clamp(x, 0, 100);
 6       b := max(100, min(x, 0));
   |
   = note: `min_max` is `deny` by default
   = note: see https://jacket.matteopolak.com/lint-rules/min_max

error[min_max]: this is always `100`: the bounds are swapped
  --> tests/lint/min_max/bad.jai:6:10
   |
 6 |     b := max(100, min(x, 0));
   |          ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
help: to keep a value between 0 and 100, write `clamp(value, 0, 100)`
   |
 5       a := min(0, max(100, x));
 6 ~     b := clamp(x, 0, 100);
 7       print("% %\n", a, b);
   |
   = note: `min_max` is `deny` by default
   = note: see https://jacket.matteopolak.com/lint-rules/min_max

error[min_max]: this is always `0`: the bounds are swapped
  --> tests/lint/min_max/bad.jai:22:12
   |
22 |     return smallest(0, largest(100, n));
   |            ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
help: to keep a value between 0 and 100, write `clamp(value, 0, 100)`
   |
21   noted_extrema :: (n: int) -> int {
22 ~     return clamp(n, 0, 100);
23   }
   |
   = note: `min_max` is `deny` by default
   = note: see https://jacket.matteopolak.com/lint-rules/min_max
